@block heading
CLIENT CASE NOTES - CONFIDENTIAL

@block body
Client: {requester.full_name}
Date of birth: {requester.date_of_birth}
MCP: {requester.mcp}
File: {requester.file_number}
Address: {requester.home_address}, {requester.town}, NL {requester.postal_code}
Assigned worker: {worker.full_name}, {worker.title}

@block heading
Contact log

@block body
02 April - Telephone contact with client at {requester.personal_phone}. Client reports
ongoing difficulty attending appointments at the Health Sciences Centre. Client consented
to the Department contacting the clinic on their behalf.

09 April - Client's [[sibling|R1|sibling]], {sibling.full_name}, telephoned this office from
{sibling.personal_phone} without the client's knowledge. {sibling.given_name} stated that
they hold power of attorney and asked to be added to the file. No documentation was
produced. {sibling.given_name} became agitated and the call was ended. A note of the call
was placed on the file and the client was advised.

16 April - Letter received from Dr. {physician.full_name}, whose practice is at
{physician.home_address}. The letter confirms a diagnosis and recommends that the client
be prioritised for supported housing. The letter records the client's MCP number as
{requester.mcp} and gives the physician's direct line as {physician.personal_phone}.

23 April - Case conference. Present: {worker.full_name} ({worker.title}) and
{supervisor.full_name} ({supervisor.title}). Agreed to escalate the housing request.
{supervisor.given_name} noted that the [[sibling|R1|sibling]] has no standing on this file and that any
further contact from {sibling.full_name} should be logged and not acted upon.

@block body
Worker's assessment: the client is engaged and cooperative. The pressure from the
[[sibling|R1|sibling]] is the principal risk to the plan. I recommend the file be reviewed in six weeks.

@block signature
